🎬 Movie Recommendation System

A content-based Movie Recommendation System built using Machine Learning, Streamlit, and TMDB API.
The app recommends movies similar to a selected movie and displays their posters using real-time API calls.

🚀 Live Demo
👉 https://movie-recommendation-system-by-bhatt.onrender.com

📌 Features
1 - 🔍 Recommend Top 5 similar movies
2 - 🤖 Uses Cosine Similarity on movie features
3 - 🎞 Fetches real-time posters from TMDB API
4 - 🖼 Graceful fallback for missing posters
5 - ⚡ Fast performance using Streamlit caching
6- 🌐 Fully deployable on Render 


🛠 Tech Stack

Python
Streamlit – Web UI
Pandas – Data handling
Scikit-learn – Similarity computation
TMDB API – Movie posters & metadata
Hugging Face Hub – Model & data storage

🧠 How It Works 

1. A **movie similarity matrix** is precomputed using cosine similarity.
2. User selects a movie from the dropdown.
3. The system:
   * Finds the selected movie index
   * Sorts similarity scores
   * Picks the top 5 most similar movies
4. Posters are fetched using **TMDB API**
5. If a poster is missing, a default placeholder image is shown (no crashes).


## ☁️ Deployment Notes

* `.pkl` files are loaded from Hugging Face for deployment safety
* Environment variables are required on the cloud
* Poster rendering is fully **null-safe**

🏆 What I Learned

* Handling **real-world API failures**
* Writing **production-safe Streamlit apps**
* Managing secrets using environment variables
* Deploying ML apps on cloud platforms


